{
  "activity_uuid": "activity_46ddb5ef-62f6-5ffb-9d21-adaf07487e34",
  "name": "13.3 Multiplying a fraction by a fraction",
  "activity_type": "TYPE_DYNAMIC",
  "activity_sub_type": "SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE",
  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Multiplying a fraction by a fraction"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Learning objective: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use the area model and multiply numerators and denominators, cancelling common factors."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Understand the concept"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In an area model, divide a unit rectangle into equal columns for one fraction and equal rows for the other. The overlap represents their product. For a/b × c/d, multiply a by c and b by d, then simplify."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cross-cancellation is valid because the whole expression is a product of fractions: divide any numerator and any denominator by a shared nonzero factor. Multiplying by a proper positive fraction less than 1 reduces a positive quantity. Multiplying by 1 leaves it unchanged; multiplying by zero gives zero."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockMathEquation",
        "attrs": {
          "math_equation": "\\frac{a}{b}\\times\\frac{c}{d}=\\frac{ac}{bd}"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "blockImage",
        "attrs": {
          "blockObject": {
            "block_uuid": "block_6380a45f-75e8-5ac3-8d1d-a66e9eb84f43",
            "content": {
              "file_id": "d4ef5c8d-7792-5eda-9852-e90be5b95628",
              "file_format": "png",
              "activity_uuid": "activity_46ddb5ef-62f6-5ffb-9d21-adaf07487e34"
            }
          },
          "size": {
            "width": 725
          },
          "alignment": "center",
          "unsplash_url": null,
          "unsplash_photographer_name": null,
          "unsplash_photographer_url": null,
          "unsplash_photo_url": null
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The overlap of three quarters of the columns and two thirds of the rows covers six of twelve cells."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked examples"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 1: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Calculate 3/5 × 5/9."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cancel 5, then 3/9 = 1/3."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 2: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A rectangular plot is 3/4 m by 2/3 m. Find its area."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "3/4 × 2/3 = 1/2 m²."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Independent practice"
